WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.750
In Chennai, homes, hospitals and emergency

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.320
services depend on connected networks.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.030
ORCA explores how an emulated satellite

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.570
backed network can protect these everyday

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.220
services.

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:14.950
An attacker uses stolen credentials to

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.850
reach the satellite operator’s ground

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.200
management network.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.200
Terminals are disrupted.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:22.590
A backup path may also be

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.150
unsafe, and service providers need to

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:25.640
be told.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.640
ORCA collects telemetry and prepares features.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:32.040
Model one detects anomalies.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.160
Model two forecasts failure in minutes.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:38.460
Model three distinguishes faults from attacks,

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:39.740
or abstains.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.980
Model four allocates limited capacity.

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:47.100
Role agents coordinate around the evidence.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.930
Retrieval searches the knowledge base for

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:50.780
relevant sources.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.170
A deterministic rule engine applies verified

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:55.680
records and returns cited verdicts.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:58.270
The agents explain; the human remains

00:00:58.270 --> 00:00:58.860
accountable.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:04.350
Before a fix, ORCA checks the

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.610
backup path and tests the plan

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:07.240
in a clone.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:10.170
In assisted mode, a human approves

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.360
the exact plan.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.200
The change rolls out in stages:

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.410
five, twenty five, then one hundred

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:16.980
percent.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.650
Re-attack checks and rollback guard the

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.080
result.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.870
Services can recover while a hash

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.720
chained audit preserves the evidence.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.550
The gap analyst records potential policy

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:30.920
gaps for human review.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:35.210
Models detect, agents coordinate, code

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:37.440
decides, and humans approve.
